<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osei Kwadwo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1764–<a href="/years/1777">1777</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osei Kwadwo was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asantehene">Asantehene</a>, or ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>, from 1764 to 1777. He introduced administrative reforms that based appointments on merit rather than solely on hereditary right. These reforms strengthened the central government's capacity to rule an increasingly complex territorial system.</p></div>
